          "case_name": "Rogers v. County of San Joaquin",
          "citation": "487 F.3d 1288 (9th Cir. 2007)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit",
          "year": 2007,
          "date_decided": "2007-05-29",
          "holding": "A social worker who removed children without a warrant was denied qualified immunity because no exigency existed; the agency's own decision to treat the report as a non-emergency ten-day response, and its ability to obtain a warrant within hours, defeated any claim of imminent danger.",
          "relevance": "Establishes that a screening decision treating a report as non-urgent is admissible against the agency on the exigency question.",
          "quote": "Here, the concerned officials classified the case as a ten-day response, indicating that they did not think that any exigency existed.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/3048851/rogers-v-county-of-san-joaquin/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 3048851
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Rowan B. v. State, Department of Health & Social Services, Office of Children's Services",
          "citation": "320 P.3d 1152 (Alaska 2014)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Alaska",
          "year": 2014,
          "date_decided": "2014-03-21",
          "holding": "Civil discovery rules, not the Public Records Act exemptions, govern a CINA parent's request for law-enforcement records, and the trial court erred by denying the request outright instead of conducting an in camera review.",
          "relevance": "Gives parents a discovery route to the screening and report records that explain why matters were opened or closed.",
          "quote": "We hold that the trial court erred in denying Rowan access to materials he sought through discovery without at least conducting an in camera review.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2657600/rowan-b-v-state-dept-of-health-social-services-office-of-children-s/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 2657600
        },
